From: yurika-sudo <yurika0uu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mm/page_alloc: floor min_free_kbytes at 64MB and lock sysctl
 to read-only (sapphire 8GB)

Stock formula value for 8GB is 11.5MB (16*sqrt(lowmem_kbytes)). Android
burst allocations (bitmap decode, GPU buffers) blow through the resulting
watermarks and push app threads into direct reclaim:

- measured on r144 over ~8h normal use: 7,790 allocstall events,
  1.2M pages scanned by app threads (pgscan_direct delta,
  bench-results/p5_before_B1.txt)
- benchmark with 64MB floor: 480MB synthetic burst produced ZERO
  allocstall and zero direct-reclaim pages — kswapd handled all of it
  in background (bench-results/p5_B1_result.txt)

- mm/page_alloc.c: user_min_free_kbytes boot default -1 -> 65536;
  calculate_min_free_kbytes() prefers this value whenever higher than
  the formula, so it acts as an immune floor (larger-RAM formula values
  still apply above it)
- kernel/sysctl.c: min_free_kbytes sysctl mode 0644 -> 0444; same
  rationale as swappiness and watermark_scale_factor locks — prevents
  ROM init.rc from overwriting the tuned value at boot

- No upstream reference: device-specific tuning, no Linux origin

Signed-off-by: yurika-sudo <yurika0uu@gmail.com>
---
 kernel/sysctl.c | 2 +-
 mm/page_alloc.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sysctl.c b/kernel/sysctl.c
index e20878716253..c1a2b9f0d1e7c 100644
--- a/kernel/sysctl.c
+++ b/kernel/sysctl.c
@@ -2908,7 +2908,7 @@ static struct ctl_table vm_table[] = {
 		.procname	= "min_free_kbytes",
 		.data		= &min_free_kbytes,
 		.maxlen		= sizeof(min_free_kbytes),
-		.mode		= 0644,
+		.mode		= 0444,
 		.proc_handler	= min_free_kbytes_sysctl_handler,
 		.extra1		= SYSCTL_ZERO,
 	},
diff --git a/mm/page_alloc.c b/mm/page_alloc.c
index de344d7c785b1..8a7c3f2e9b4d1 100644
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -437,7 +437,7 @@ compound_page_dtor * const compound_page_dtors[NR_COMPOUND_DTORS] = {
 
 int min_free_kbytes = 1024;
-int user_min_free_kbytes = -1;
+int user_min_free_kbytes = 65536;
 int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly = 0;
 int watermark_scale_factor = 30;
 
